course: dictionary
lesson: 2100
title: Continuous: going on without a break
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Continuous comes from continue. It means going on without stopping, or with no gaps at all. Think of continuous rain that does not stop for a minute, or a continuous line drawn without lifting your pen.
explain: Look at the words around it to find the meaning. In «They hear the long continuous drone of the Badger's voice, rising and falling in waves», a drone that goes on and on without stopping is continuous. The word long is a clue too.
explain: Continuous also has special jobs in English and maths. In grammar it is a verb form, be plus an -ing verb, as in «I am reading». In maths, continuous data can take any value in a range, like height, while counted data, like the number of pets, uses whole numbers.
fact: Continuous means going on without stopping or breaking.
fact: Continuous can also mean without gaps or spaces, as in a continuous line.
fact: The continuous form of a verb uses be plus an -ing verb, such as «I am reading».
fact: The future continuous is «will be» plus an -ing verb: «I will be swimming at 3 o'clock tomorrow».
fact: In maths, continuous data can take any value in a range, like height or time, so it is measured, not counted.
exercise: «The continuous rain soaked everyone at the match.» What does continuous mean here? | Bright and sunny | *Going on without stopping | Small and quick | Very loud
exercise: Which phrase shows the continuous form of a verb? | «I read books» | *«I am reading» | «Reading is fun» | «The book is red»
exercise: Which of these is continuous data, not counted in whole numbers? | Number of children | *Height | Number of books | Number of pets
test: Which phrase means without gaps or spaces? | A broken line | A dotted line | A zigzag line | *A continuous line
test: Which words fill the gap? «I ___ swimming at 3 o'clock tomorrow.» | *will be | are | have | was
exam: Which sentence shows a continuous action happening now? | The dog barked yesterday | *The dog is barking now | The dog bark | The dog's bark was loud
